WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.120
Every sale starts as someone seeing you.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.260
Most of them never get to the end.

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.020
Where do they go?

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.040
The funnel, and what a sale costs.

5
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.670
The funnel is made up of the actions

6
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.760
your potential customers have to take.

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.000
Impression: the ad, the result, the post is seen.

8
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.240
One hundred percent.

9
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.040
Engagement: a click. The first action they take.

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:29.600
Eight percent.

11
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.020
Action: a form, a call, a step into the site.

12
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.540
Two percent.

13
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.940
Goal fulfilled: the conversion that pays for it all.

14
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.980
Zero point six percent.

15
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.360
These rates are illustrative.

16
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.500
The shape is not.

17
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.420
Every extra step you add loses people,

18
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.020
so a step has to earn its place.

19
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.180
Now work it backwards.

20
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.340
You need six sales.

21
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:56.800
How many impressions

22
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.460
does the top of the funnel need?

23
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.720
Six sales, at zero point six percent,

24
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.000
is a thousand impressions.

25
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.280
And that is how a media budget gets sized.

26
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.620
All traffic sources bring value.

27
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.300
Every one of them.

28
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.700
Every traffic source has a cost,

29
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.460
including the ones that look free.

30
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.300
Content costs time,

31
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.060
and time costs money.

32
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.260
Operate by a clear economic model,

33
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.840
or you cannot tell a good channel from a bad one.

34
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:28.690
If a lead costs thirty dollars,

35
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.260
and one in five leads becomes a sale,

36
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.980
a sale costs a hundred and fifty dollars in marketing.

37
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.320
If the customer is worth four hundred dollars,

38
00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.560
the channel works.

39
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.120
If they are worth a hundred and twenty,

40
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:42.960
it does not,

41
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.100
no matter how good the creative is.

42
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.420
Understand this one calculation,

43
00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.620
and you can hold a conversation with a finance director.

44
00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.020
Next, work the funnel backwards

45
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.260
with your own numbers.

